Unpeel: pack page metadata ahead of the cell array (lazy-resident cells).

Why: docs/plans/pty-core.md, 'Round 4, Lane 2'. Page memory comes from
mmap (zeroed, unresident) and only the bytes init WRITES become resident.
Init writes the row headers and every metadata region (style set table
and items, grapheme/string allocator bitmaps, map metadata, hyperlink set)
but never the cells. Upstream lays out rows, then the 55 KiB cell array,
then the metadata, so on macOS (16 KiB pages) those init writes touch
OS pages far apart and an EMPTY 80x24 terminal committed 81 KiB in its
first page alone. With metadata first and cells last the init writes
share one or two OS pages and the untouched cell array stays unresident
until output arrives. Offsets are only ever read from Page.Layout, so no
consumer changes; availableBitsForGrid uses the equivalent front-of-page
formula. Applied only when building the vendored libghostty-vt.a for
unpeel-host (build.sh); the app's GhosttyKit build is untouched.

